e tweets hey if  we can't figure out how to replace this  thing let's just repeal Obamacare and  figure out the rest later Donald Trump  tweeting on his Twitter account if  Republican senators are unable to pass  what they are working on  they should immediately repeal and then  replace at a later date this will lead  to 32 million people losing their  insurance . i don't need to qualify it i  don't need to say anything else about it  now where do i get the number 32 million  people let's put that on record just so  you don't think I'm making this up the  Congressional Budget Office did an  analysis one of those times that  Republicans floated the idea of merely  repealing the Affordable Care Act they  determined that 32 million people nearly  10 percent of our country's population  would lose coverage by 2026 19 million  of them would lose Medicaid coverage  people already die because they don't  have health care and way more people are  going to die from lack of care if  Obamacare is repealed and replaced with  the AHCA  even more people will die if you just  repeal Obamacare what do you have left  if you just repeal Obamacare  nothing well I think this strategy is a  sly way to get Democrats on board  because you can repeal Obamacare  probably with just the Republicans in  the House and the Senate you can appeal  to the people on the far right and not  really have to grab the moderates as  well and then when there's that interim  phase while Obamacare is phasing out  slowly then Democrats may be guilted  into joining on board and passing  something similar to what they have now  which is the American health care it's  possible but the timing of that has to  be so perfect for Republicans to not get  crushed in 2018 and or 2020 I mean  you're basically threading a needle  where you're saying we've got to start  causing just enough misery that  Democrats might agree to our terms but  not so much that Republican voters hold  us accountable so it's certainly  possible but it would require such  incredible timing to do that and I  cannot possibly overstate the perversion  and the moral corruption of the  suggestion particularly from the guy who  campaigned on creating a quote beautiful  replacement to Obamacare that was going  to work for everyone  less money no one uninsured better care  the suggestion now is just get rid of  Obamacare period  the way things are going there might  never be a replacement especially if you  get Obamacare out of the way first and  then Republicans Pat might say let's  just blame Democrats for what's going on  because hey Obamacare was bad and we  repealed it and that was our campaign  promise and we did it the fact that we  haven't passed anything else let's just  blame that on Democrats even though  again it's Republicans that are  preventing them from passing it so far  well I think taking the coverage from 32  million people without any replacement  option would play terribly for  Republicans right and there's no chance  that would be able to hold the house in  2018 if they did that I hope that might  be good for Democrats but we don't sit  here and say well that would be good  overall politically for us so just screw  the people off their health insurance as  the right is doing not only that I  talked about the reversible or the  meaningless actions that Donald Trump  has taken firing certain departments  from the White House people resigning  whatever we've talked about that some of  the meaningless symbolic executive  orders we've talked about that this  would not be one of them right to the  extent that Donald Trump is supportive  of Republicans in the House and Senate  saying just a straight-up repeal of  Obamacare that would not be one of the  reversible actions of Donald Trump and  Republicans if you care about net  neutrality consider this an attack on  net neutrality because if you're sick  and you've got no health care that  becomes your priority not activating  around net neutrality if you care about  education consider this suggestion from  Donald Trump and attack on education  because if you're sick and have no  health care it's hard to be working on  education if you care about the  environment consider this suggestion and  attack on the environment because if  you're sick and have no health care that  is your priority day to day not the  environment these are straight-up liars  Democrats and Republicans are the same  on many issues and when they are I call  them out for it not here not this one  they said the Republicans said this  isn't about political points from just  repealing Obamacare we want to replace  Obamacare with something that works for  everyone  then why is anyone talking about a  straight repeal as a possible good idea  it is discussed  do not allow this to be normalized and  by the way who is my representative calm  whether you're a Democrat or a  Republican  whether you're represented by a Democrat  or a Republican this is an issue where  you have to make your voice heard and  we're going to be covering this until we  have some kind of resolution on it

